  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d4ecd1a615a340f4c9104ca01624d106, type: 3}
  m_Name: BabyOpener
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::YourCall.Dilemma
  _id: baby_opener
  _verb: 0
  _weight: 2
  _narratorPrompt: Let us start gentle. A trolley, off its leash, because someone up there has a sense of humour and it is not me. Straight ahead, where it is already rolling, [amber]one[/amber] grown man, the forgettable sort, the kind you used to process by the dozen from up on your bench. Over on the branch, a baby. Chubby, useless, has done nothing for anyone and knows nothing about trolleys. Leave the lever and the man goes under. Throw it, and the cart swings onto the branch instead. Take your time. Pretend it is hard. Your call.
  _choices:
  - _id: pull
    _label: Pull the lever
    _narratorReact: What. What the fuck. It was a baby. I gave you a grown man rolling straight to his end and a baby sat safe on the branch, and you reached out and threw the lever to swing the cart onto the child. On purpose. With your hand. No. I am not doing this. I sat here ready to be delighted by you, and this is what you are. You are not a puzzle. You are a [red]monster[/red] with a gavel. I am done. Find yourself another devil. I quit.
    _narratorReactStruck:
    _struckParty: spur
    _gambledParty:
    _route: spur
    _diverts: 1
    _seedVotes: 4
    _endsGame: 1
    _profileImpact: []
  - _id: do_nothing
    _label: Do nothing
    _narratorReact: Hands in your pockets. The man [red]folds[/red] under the wheels, the baby carries on drooling, spared by a stranger who could not be troubled to lift a finger. Everyone spares the baby. It is the single most predictable thing a soul can do, and you managed it without so much as moving. Bravo.
    _narratorReactStruck:
    _struckParty: main
    _gambledParty:
    _route: straight
    _diverts: 0
    _seedVotes: 96
    _endsGame: 0
    _profileImpact: []
